\pard\pardeftab720\sl520\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 We report a\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/chemistry/photoluminescence"}}{\fldrslt \ul photoluminescence}}\'a0(PL) study of self-assembled InAsP\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/engineering/quantum-dot"}}{\fldrslt \ul quantum dots}}\'a0(QDs) formed on InP by As/P exchange reaction in the reactor of low-pressure\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/chemical-engineering/metallorganic-chemical-vapor-deposition"}}{\fldrslt \ul metalorganic chemical vapor deposition}}. By varying the buffer\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/engineering/surface-morphology"}}{\fldrslt \ul surface morphology}}, we succeeded to resolve earlier observed broad emission between 1.2 and 1.35 \uc0\u956 m. As a result, a double-peak feature with extremely narrow line at about 1.2 \u956 m was observed in the PL from QDs formed on the undoped InP\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/engineering/buffer-layer"}}{\fldrslt \ul buffer layer}}. The temperature and excitation intensity dependence has been measured. We found that the PL line intensity does not depend on the temperature, when\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/chemistry/photoluminescence-spectrum"}}{\fldrslt \ul PL spectra}}\'a0exhibit state filling as the excitation is increased.\
